spec.task:
Write a small command-line front end for a sudoku module that already exists and is importable as `sudoku_core`, sitting in the same directory.

`sudoku_core` provides: solve(grid) which fills the grid IN PLACE and returns True, generate(), is_valid(grid, row, col, value), and format_grid(grid).

The front end must:
  - print a freshly generated puzzle;
  - loop reading lines of the form `row col value` (1-9 each), rejecting a move that is_valid() refuses, and reprinting the grid after each accepted move;
  - accept `solve` to fill the grid in and `quit` to exit;
  - say so and exit when the grid is complete;
  - do all of that under `if __name__ == "__main__":` so importing it runs nothing.

Use only the standard library. Keep it under 80 lines.

Your entire response must be the Python source and nothing else: no explanation, no markdown fences, no ``` anywhere.
